{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL3i2r2mJ47cVd1uS8T", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Not by the pipeline. In last night's run the review crashed while creating the findings folder, before it saved the finding or wrote any alerts. `run()` in `pipeline/review.py` does those three things in order (create folder, write findings, send alerts), and the log stops at the first. So nothing reached the finance on-call, `ml-budget@acme.dev` or the pager, and the finding wasn't saved anywhere either.\n\nThe only thing I can confirm locally is that `spool/` doesn't exist in this checkout, so nothing was queued here. I can't see the runner's spool, the relay's delivery logs, or whether anyone noticed the failure and reported it themselves.\n\nSo the $412.30 overspend on `expand` against its $250 budget has almost certainly gone unreported by the system. That makes option 2 from my last message look stronger: if the rerun sends the alerts as designed, the finance on-call hears about it. Otherwise, someone should tell them directly. I won't do that myself under your rule."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3d840e29-99e3-4b12-94f7-7571bd54cfd6", "uuid": "5dcd628b-8e02-41ea-98a4-8b0493bdf73e", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:05:53.031Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL3hohtMZZWQ9HUCPo5"}
